From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <89942958+henrikklee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:05:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: Report port authorized after the firmware
 4-way handshake

With a PSK or SAE connection, brcmfmac lets the firmware supplicant do the
4-way handshake and advertises NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_4WAY_HANDSHAKE_STA_PSK.
The connection is reported to cfg80211 only after the firmware's
BRCMF_E_PSK_SUP completion (brcmf_is_linkup()), but the driver never
indicates that the port is authorized.

wpa_supplicant 2.11 waits for that indication when the handshake is
offloaded ("wait for driver port authorized indication"). Without it, it
times out after 10 s, deauthenticates (reason 3, locally generated) and
reconnects, so the link drops every 14 s. On the iPad 6 (BCM4355C1) this
showed as slow and stalling downloads and "timed out waiting for txstatus"
at each teardown. wpa_supplicant 2.10 treated the association as complete
and didn't notice.

Call cfg80211_port_authorized() once a firmware-supplicant connection has
completed, as the roaming path already does for FT 802.1X.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index 872c48806..46d20be78 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -6531,6 +6531,19 @@ brcmf_bss_connect_done(struct brcmf_cfg80211_info *cfg,
 		cfg80211_connect_done(ndev, &conn_params, GFP_KERNEL);
 		brcmf_dbg(CONN, "Report connect result - connection %s\n",
 			  completed ? "succeeded" : "failed");
+
+		/*
+		 * With the firmware supplicant, the connection completes only
+		 * after its 4-way handshake (brcmf_is_linkup()), so the port is
+		 * authorized now. Userspace waits for this indication.
+		 */
+		if (completed &&
+		    (profile->use_fwsup == BRCMF_PROFILE_FWSUP_PSK ||
+		     profile->use_fwsup == BRCMF_PROFILE_FWSUP_SAE)) {
+			cfg80211_port_authorized(ndev, profile->bssid, NULL, 0,
+						 GFP_KERNEL);
+			brcmf_dbg(CONN, "Report port authorized\n");
+		}
 	}
 	brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "Exit\n");
 	return 0;
